187 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (The Maulana Azad National Institute of Technology \(MANIT\), Bhopal, is one of India's premier technical institutions and an Institute of National Importance under the NIT Act. Established in 1960 as one of the country's first Regional Engineering Colleges, the institute was upgraded to a National Institute of Technology in 2002. Situated on a sprawling 650-acre green campus in the heart of Bhopal, the capital city of Madhya Pradesh. MANIT has emerged as a distinguished centre for excellence in engineering, technology, architecture, planning, management, and scientific research.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
188 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (Committed to academic excellence, innovation, and societal development, MANIT offers a wide range of undergraduate, postgraduate, and doctoral programmes across diverse disciplines. The institute fosters a vibrant research ecosystem through interdisciplinary collaboration, industry partnerships, and international engagement. With its state-of-the-art infrastructure, accomplished faculty, and dynamic student community, MANIT continues to contribute significantly to technological advancement, knowledge creation, and nation-building.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
